  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">2022 - Develop national strategies through preparatory visits and stakeholder workshops</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of national strategies developed</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3 - Afghanistan, Iraq and Sri Lanka</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">GICHD organised a strategy stakeholder workshop in Colombo in June 2022, bringing together all mine action programme stakeholders. The workshop allowed participants to gain clarity on achievements and challenges in implementing the previous national mine action strategy, identify key strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats faced by the programme and develop a Theory of Change for the next strategic period. GICHD presented the results to the Government of Sri Lanka and International Donors at the high-level workshop closure, which brought National Government and international donors firmly onboard. 
GICHD will continue to monitor the situation in Sri Lanka in light of the recent events and changes in Government and plans to visit the country again in quarter 4 in 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-03-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">GICHD visited Baghdad, Fallujah and Erbil in March 2022, to agree on next steps regarding the finalization and implementation of the 2022-2028 Iraq National Mine Action Strategy and visit operations. Together with the Dutch Embassy in Baghdad, GICHD organized a donor meeting which was hosted at the Dutch Embassy. GICHD briefed donors on the strategic planning process and issues related to national ownership and localisation were discussed. A trilateral meeting was then held between the Dutch Ambassador and First Secretary, DMA&apos;s Director General and GICHD, at DMA&apos;s office, on the strategy approval process, among other subjects.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-09-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3"></target>
     <actual value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sri Lanka 2023-2027 Completion Strategy mainstreams gender and diversity in all strategic objectives. All relevant outcome indicators disaggregate data in a sex-, age- and disability disaggregated manner. 
The Strategy has now formally been validated by all relevant stakeholders and will be approved by relevant Ministry representatives in the last quarter of 2022. It is expected to enter into force on 1 January 2023.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-10-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3"></target>
     <actual value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Sri Lanka&apos;s Strategy mainstreams gender and diversity in all strategic objectives. All relevant outcome indicators disaggregate data in a sex-, age- and disability disaggregated manner.
The Strategy is expected to be approved by the Government of Sri Lanka in early 2023.&quot;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of national strategies that integrate gender and diversity considerations</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3 - Afghanistan, Iraq and Sri Lanka</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">GICHD organised a strategy stakeholder workshop in Colombo in June 2022, bringing together all mine action programme stakeholders. The workshop allowed participants to gain clarity on achievements and challenges in implementing the previous national mine action strategy, identify key strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats faced by the programme and develop a Theory of Change for the next strategic period. GICHD presented the results to the Government of Sri Lanka and International Donors at the high-level workshop closure, which brought National Government and international donors firmly onboard. 
GICHD will continue to monitor the situation in Sri Lanka in light of the recent events and changes in Government and plans to visit the country again in quarter 4 in 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-09-30"></period-end>
     <target value="3"></target>
     <actual value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">GICHD supported Sri Lanka&apos;s National Mine Action Centre (NMAC) in the development of its 2023-2027 Completion strategy, following a strategy stakeholder workshop in June 2022 which led to the elaboration of a Theory of Change. In September 2022, GICHD and NMAC organized a strategy validation workshop in Colombo to validate the draft strategy with all relevant stakeholders. GICHD observed a high level of collaboration and engagement from all stakeholders, despite continued difficult times faced by the country due to the financial crisis and inflation.
The Strategy has now formally been validated by all relevant stakeholders and will be approved by relevant Ministry representatives in the last quarter of 2022. It is expected to enter into force on 1 January 2023.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-10-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3"></target>
     <actual value="2">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The GICHD continued to support Sri Lanka&apos;s National Mine Action Centre (NMAC) in Q4 2022. The GICHD-supported National Mine Action Completion Strategy 2023-2027, was validated by all main stakeholders at a GICHD-facilitated workshop in Colombo in September 2022, but still awaits official approval by the Government of Sri Lanka as of early 2023.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
